# an f32 x/y measured as a GPU makes it (#29): Vulkan gives OpFDiv 2.5
# ulp, so the rationals' errors are the worst of the correctly rounded
# quotient and two floats to either side; the reciprocal with one fma
# correction (horner+rcp) brings the quotient back to about half an ulp
approx tan(x) in -1.2..1.2 ulp 3 nosplit noreduce list 3
# a looser target: the plain division meets it, cheaper
approx tan(x) in -1.2..1.2 ulp 6 nosplit noreduce list 2
